              "instruction": "the cousins — \"sí, sì, sim\" — all from Latin sīc",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: the cousins — \"sí, sì, sim\" — all from Latin *sīc*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "How do you say yes in Spanish? (sí.) What is the only difference between sí \"yes\" and si \"if\"? (The written accent.) What Latin word is sí from, and what did it mean? (sīc — \"thus, so\".)"
            }
          ]
        }
